# pkg-config template for libfasm_capi (rust/fasm-capi), the C and C++
# (header-only, include/fasm/fasm.hpp) API of the fasm library.
#
# Substituted and installed by `make capi-install PREFIX=...` (see
# Makefile) into $(PREFIX)/lib/pkgconfig/fasm.pc: the three placeholders
# below (prefix path, version, private link libraries) are filled in from
# the install prefix, the crate version (rust/fasm-capi/Cargo.toml, i.e.
# the workspace root Cargo.toml) and the system libraries the static
# library needs (see rust/fasm-capi/tests/c/CMakeLists.txt's
# FASM_NATIVE_LIBS, from `cargo rustc -p fasm-capi -- --print
# native-static-libs`). Do not use the placeholder syntax anywhere else in
# this file (a plain `sed` substitutes every occurrence).
#
# `pkg-config --cflags --libs fasm` gives a dynamically linked build
# (`-lfasm_capi`, needing libfasm_capi.so at run time, e.g. via
# LD_LIBRARY_PATH or an rpath). Both the C header and the C++ wrapper are
# reached through the same Cflags (-I${includedir}, giving <fasm/fasm.h>
# and <fasm/fasm.hpp>); the C++ wrapper needs no extra library (header
# only). Verified (rust/fasm-capi/examples/cpp):
#
#   g++ -std=c++17 $(pkg-config --cflags fasm) example.cpp \
#       $(pkg-config --libs fasm) -o example
#   LD_LIBRARY_PATH=${libdir} ./example
#
# To link `libfasm_capi.a` instead (no run time dependency on the .so),
# `pkg-config --static --libs fasm` is *not* enough on its own: pkg-config
# has no notion of "this Libs entry means the static archive", so it
# still emits plain `-lfasm_capi` (picked up as the .so by a linker that
# has both available) followed by `Libs.private`'s system libraries
# (there is no `--libs.private` pkg-config option; `--static --libs` /
# `--static --libs-only-l` is how Libs.private is reached). Force the one
# `-lfasm_capi` from `Libs` to resolve against the archive with
# `-Wl,-Bstatic` / `-Wl,-Bdynamic` around it, switching back to dynamic
# before the private system libraries (which are typically only
# available as shared objects). Verified:
#
#   g++ -std=c++17 $(pkg-config --cflags fasm) example.cpp \
#       -Wl,-Bstatic $(pkg-config --libs fasm) \
#       -Wl,-Bdynamic $(pkg-config --static --libs-only-l fasm | sed 's/-lfasm_capi//') \
#       -o example_static
#
# (`ldd example_static` then shows no libfasm_capi.so dependency.) The
# CMake FASM_STATIC path in rust/fasm-capi/tests/c/CMakeLists.txt links
# the static library the same way, without pkg-config, by naming
# libfasm_capi.a's path directly as an IMPORTED target.

prefix=@PREFIX@
exec_prefix=${prefix}
includedir=${prefix}/include
libdir=${prefix}/lib

Name: fasm
Description: FASM (FPGA Assembly) parsing, model, output and merge library: C API (fasm/fasm.h) and header-only C++17 RAII wrapper (fasm/fasm.hpp)
Version: @VERSION@
Libs: -L${libdir} -lfasm_capi
Libs.private: @LIBS_PRIVATE@
Cflags: -I${includedir}
